    "title": "Former Kmart on Vivion Road Could Become $100M VA Clinic - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Marcus Vance ,\n2 days ago A Kmart that has sat empty on NE Vivion Road since 2014 could soon become a VA outpatient clinic, if the Kansas City Area Transportation Authority can move forward with its proposal. The agency bought the 16.4-acre site in 2022, and now the long-vacant big-box store is at the center of a redevelopment proposal that could bring a facility worth between $85 million and $100 million to the Northland. Read full article\n18",
